From 82ef3e69aacbafe12b5d463b84a5d6e3e9422be2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:18:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 86/91] fix(websocket): never log while holding the connection
 lock, and let one large message through

With the hub log sink installed, every log line is sent to /logs/stream
subscribers through send_json, which takes connections_mutex_. Three
warnings were logged while that lock was held: a connection over the
outbound queue bound, an oversized message, and a refused connection.
Any of them deadlocked lemond while a log subscriber was connected.
They are now collected under the lock and logged after it is released.

An empty queue now always accepts the next message, so a large
logs.snapshot no longer closes a client that is keeping up.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
